@startuml agentic-vs-autonomous-system
title Agentic vs Autonomous System Orthogonality ; per ADR-ES-025 section 8 + ADR-ES-022 section 13

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class "System" as Sys
class "Agentic System" as ASys
class "Autonomous System candidate" as AuSys

Sys <|-- ASys : specializes (v2.3.0, Established)
Sys <|-- AuSys : specialization deferred

note bottom of Sys
  Per ADR-ES-022 section 13 (mechanical symmetry
  prohibition) + ADR-ES-025 section 13:
  Autonomous System is intentionally NOT
  established alongside Agentic System.
  A separate semantic decision is required.

  Per ADR-ES-025 section 8 four-state model:
  - Conventional System (no agentic, no autonomous)
  - Agentic System (yes agentic, no autonomous)
  - Autonomous System candidate (no agentic, yes autonomous) - DEFERRED
  - Agentic + Autonomous System candidate - DEFERRED
end note

@enduml
